{
  "version": 2,
  "purpose": "Map technician/colloquial vocabulary to the manual's formal ECU terminology, to close the symptom-retrieval vocabulary gap (Phase 8.2, limitation L1).",
  "rules": [
    "Aliases are SUBSYSTEM-level (system_aliases, applied to every record of that system) or DESCRIPTION-level (term_synonyms, applied only when the manual term appears in a record's description, optionally restricted to listed systems). They are NEVER derived from step text: step boilerplate is shared across hundreds of DTCs, and aliasing it would re-collapse near-duplicates.",
    "Index side: a record's alias string = colloquial terms of its system + colloquial terms of every term_synonym triggered by its description.",
    "Query side: every colloquial term found in the query (word-boundary, longest first) is expanded by appending its manual terms.",
    "provenance: general = standard technician synonym authored from the manual's own vocabulary before inspecting any 8.2 retrieval output; user = specified in the Phase 8.2 brief; dev_driven = added after inspecting a DEV miss.",
    "matches_dev_query / matches_test_query are COMPUTED from gold query text (src/lexicon.py audit), never hand-set. TEST-matching entries are ablated at 8.5 to give an uncontaminated TEST lower bound.",
    "v2: an alias stays SUBSYSTEM-level only if it is correct for EVERY record in that subsystem. Where a subsystem mixes components (engine_position = crank + cam; dpf_regen = DPF + DOC; fuel_supply = pump + temperature sensor + metering unit; o2_exhaust = NOx + exhaust-temperature; pedal_clutch_brake = pedal + clutch + brake), the alias is DESCRIPTION-level instead, so a camshaft record never receives crank aliases."
  ],
